{
  "body" : "You are designing a moody urban illustration with a melancholic and introspective tone.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n- Primary subject: {{subject}}\n- Backdrop: {{scene}}\n- Text overlay: {{copy}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n- Genre / medium: Atmospheric hand-drawn urban illustration.\n- Composition: Tall portrait aspect (~1024×1536); subject placed in lower foreground with tangled wires spreading across the frame.\n- Lens / camera: Illustrative perspective with exaggerated vertical depth and no defined focal compression.\n- Lighting: Diffuse, overcast lighting with muted tonal gradients; soft shadows and no direct highlights.\n- Color palette and grading: Muted grayscale with subtle green and beige undertones; desaturated and somber.\n- Texture / surface: Visible brushstrokes and sketch-like linework; slightly gritty and painterly.\n- Post-processing: Light smudging and texture overlays to enhance the raw, weathered aesthetic.\n- Mood: Melancholic, bleak, introspective.\n- References: Studio Ghibli's urban sketches, Edward Hopper's atmospheric isolation, modern graphic novels with urban themes.\n- Mood adjustment: {{mood}}\n\nDESIGN RULES\n- Aspect: 2:3 portrait (~1024×1536) suitable for editorial or narrative art placement.\n- Maintain a balance between negative space and intricate wire details.\n- Ensure foreground subject contrasts subtly against the background texture without overpowering the scene.\n\nAVOID\n- Overly bright or saturated colors.\n- Dynamic, energetic poses or expressions.\n- Busy compositions that obscure the wires and subject.\n- Flat or overly clean textures.\n- High-contrast lighting.\n- Artificial or digital-looking elements.\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nSubject: {{subject}}\nSetting: {{scene}}\nCopy: {{copy}}\nMood adjustment: {{mood}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}",
